{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2150-02-13 17:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be your doctor during this stay. You’re here for abdominal pain, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2150-02-13 17:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it’s that same pain I always get—epigastric, radiating to my back. Started two days ago with nausea and vomiting, now just dry heaving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2150-02-13 17:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You’ve had this many times before. We’ll treat it like your usual pancreatitis flare. We’ll start IV fluids and your regular pain and nausea meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2150-02-13 17:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I tried extra IV hydration at home last week and avoided admission, but this time it’s worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2150-02-13 17:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing your best. We’ll get you comfortable. Your labs came back—lipase is normal, but that doesn’t rule out a flare given your history."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2150-02-13 17:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I know it’s not always elevated in me. I haven’t eaten since yesterday. I usually use my J-tube for Ensure, but I haven’t touched it in two days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2150-02-13 17:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep you NPO for now and advance slowly. We’ve started your IV Dilaudid and Toradol for pain, and Zofran and Ativan for nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2150-02-13 17:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I respond well to that combo. My blood pressure was high earlier—should I be worried?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2150-02-13 17:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It was 149/106—elevated but not dangerous. We’ll continue your amlodipine and add lisinopril 10mg daily to help control it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2150-02-13 17:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I remember last time we avoided lisinopril because of pancreatitis risk, but you said amlodipine was safer."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2150-02-13 17:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’re still avoiding triggers. Lisinopril is low risk for you, and we need better BP control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2150-02-13 17:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. And my warfarin? I’m on it for my old DVT."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2150-02-13 17:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We held warfarin since you’re not eating. We started lovenox for now. We’ll recheck your INR and adjust when you’re back on oral intake."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2150-02-13 17:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. I’ve had so many line infections—I don’t want another clot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2150-02-13 17:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re being careful. Your Hickman line looks clean—no redness or tenderness. We’re doing ethanol locks twice daily to prevent infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2150-02-13 17:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I do those at home too. But I’ve been having tooth pain—could that be a problem?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2150-02-13 17:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, with a central line, dental infections can spread. We consulted oral surgery. They’ll see you tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2150-02-14 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. The oral surgeon saw you—they found significant caries, especially in tooth #8, which is broken. They recommend extractions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2150-02-14 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh no. That front tooth is broken? It’s embarrassing. But will pulling teeth be safe with my line?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2150-02-14 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "They recommend prophylactic antibiotics before any procedure. Since you’re not on anticoagulants long-term, it’s low risk. We’ll stop lovenox after discussion with your PCP."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2150-02-14 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I’m stopping lovenox? I thought I needed it for the DVT."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2150-02-14 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You completed three months for the line-associated clot. Your team agreed it’s safe to stop. We’ll monitor, but no long-term anticoagulation needed now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2150-02-14 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that’s a relief. And my migraines? They’ve been worse—maybe from the tooth pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2150-02-14 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re on Fioricet as needed. The surgeon thinks dental pain is contributing. Once that’s treated, your headaches may improve."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2150-02-14 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I hope so. And my stomach pain—is it getting better?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2150-02-14 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’ve had less nausea today. We’ll try small sips of water and see how you do."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2150-02-15 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. Pain is better, and labs show your hemoglobin is stable at 10.9—good improvement from admission."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2150-02-15 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel stronger. Can I eat something? I’m so tired of being NPO."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2150-02-15 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll start you on a clear liquid diet and advance slowly. If you tolerate it, we’ll move to soft foods like mashed potatoes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2150-02-15 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. And my meds—when do I switch back to oral?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2150-02-15 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve restarted omeprazole IV for your GERD. Once you’re eating, we’ll switch to oral. Same with amitriptyline—we’ll restart at bedtime."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2150-02-15 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been feeling down—re-admitted again, missing a tooth. It’s hard."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2150-02-15 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. The social worker spoke with you—she mentioned a care planning meeting next time if needed. But we’re here for you now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2150-02-16 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re on day three of pain control. We’re stopping IV ketorolac—just using Dilaudid as needed. How’s the pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2150-02-16 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Much better. I only took one dose yesterday. I’m eating mashed potatoes and applesauce—no nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2150-02-16 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Excellent. We’ll keep advancing your diet. Your hemoglobin is holding at 31.7%—no need for iron infusion this time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2150-02-16 08:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ve had those before—they helped. But if I don’t need it, even better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2150-02-17 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re almost ready for discharge. We’ll write prescriptions for Dilaudid, Ativan for nausea, and continue your home meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2150-02-17 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I still get IV fluids at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2150-02-17 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes—1 liter four times a week. We’re sending you home with an IV pump and instructions for ethanol locks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2150-02-17 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my dental follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2150-02-17 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll see oral surgery next week. They’ll plan extractions. Take antibiotics before any procedure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2150-02-18 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Last day on IV meds. We’re switching you fully to oral pain and nausea control. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2150-02-18 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Really good. I walked the hallway twice yesterday. I think I’m ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2150-02-18 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We agree. We’ll discharge tomorrow. We’ve updated your meds—lisinopril is now daily, and methadone is reduced to one tablet twice a day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2150-02-18 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Why the change in methadone?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2150-02-18 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You were on three tablets twice a day, but we’re simplifying to avoid over-sedation. One tablet is enough with your current pain level."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2150-02-18 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And amlodipine—now it’s 5 mg twice a day?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2150-02-18 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, split dose for better blood pressure control. You’ve been normotensive on this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2150-02-19 09:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final day. You’re tolerating a soft diet, pain is mild, and you’re up and moving. Discharge is set for tomorrow morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2150-02-19 09:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m so glad. Can I use my J-tube again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2150-02-19 09:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, when you feel like it. Continue watered-down Ensure, but only if you tolerate it. Focus on small oral meals first."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2150-02-19 09:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my line care—ethanol locks every day?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2150-02-19 09:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, two mL in each lumen daily. Lock for two hours, then flush with saline and heparin. We’ve trained the home health nurse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2150-02-20 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All set for discharge tomorrow. Your follow-up with your primary doctor is in one week. Dental in two."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2150-02-20 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if I start feeling another flare?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2150-02-20 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Start extra IV fluids, use your PRN pain and nausea meds. If vomiting persists or pain worsens, come back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2150-02-20 11:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you for everything. I’m embarrassed about my tooth, but I’ll get it fixed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2150-02-20 11:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve been through a lot. We’re here to help. Take care of yourself, and we’ll see you in clinic."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2150-02-21 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re cleared to go home. Home health will visit tomorrow to check your line and IV setup."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2150-02-21 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I feel so much better. I’ll follow up with everyone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2150-02-21 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Remember: lisinopril daily, watch for dizziness, and call if you have fever or line redness."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2150-02-21 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And thank you for listening. It means a lot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2150-02-21 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Of course. Take care. We’re here if you need us."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2150-02-13 16:43:00",
    "admission_end": "2150-02-21 17:21:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted for a flare of chronic pancreatitis, presenting with epigastric pain radiating to the back, nausea, and vomiting. She was treated with IV fluids, hydromorphone, ketorolac, and anti-nausea medications, with gradual advancement to a soft diet. Her pain and nausea improved, and she was transitioned back to oral medications. New concerns included dental caries, particularly in tooth #8, prompting a referral to oral surgery for planned extractions with antibiotic prophylaxis. Anticoagulation with lovenox was stopped after completing treatment for a prior line-associated DVT. Blood pressure was managed with continued amlodipine and addition of lisinopril. She was discharged home with home health services, instructions for Hickman line care with ethanol locks, and follow-up plans for dental and primary care.",
    "problems": [
      "Acute pancreatitis",
      "Chronic pancreatitis",
      "Iron deficiency anemia, unspecified",
      "Status of other artificial opening of gastrointestinal tract",
      "Dental caries, unspecified",
      "Migraine, unspecified, without mention of intractable migraine without mention of status migrainosus",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Personal history of venous thrombosis and embolism",
      "Long-term (current) use of anticoagulants",
      "Other genetic carrier status"
    ]
  }
}
